 true] [17592186407368 1071 "![](images/42/42e0a9a9e987c1c56a335f29cf939e4f03d496fad148f148c32377893dbe7c13.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$" 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407368 1072 #uuid "82f2815d-a760-5a7e-b3a4-18ea182996e3" 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407368 1074 "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.  \n\n- Diagram I is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. There are vectors  $a=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$  in the subset for which ${a}_{1}>0$ and ${a}_{2}>0.$   But then\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1} \\\\ -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407369 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407367 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407369 1069 "q-35574" 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407369 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407369 1071 "![](images/1d/1d5d9586684c8606ca0f6df8dd70d9828ea04d3d9097b5a155ab66bcd7300ffd.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$" 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407369 1072 #uuid "befb255b-f1bd-5c00-bc58-981c00e76ebb" 13194139533542 17592186045585 true] [17592186407369 1074 "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace.  In this case we also have that the vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\"." 13194139533542 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-368e8346-dba0-5eab-bd72-0c8e01860bad" 17592186407356 "answer-4c5b8efe-00bb-54bf-84b6-0c9423e627f4" 17592186407357 "answer-70ea133b-bffa-5ff6-b9b3-2c01068c74c9" 17592186407358 "answer-99103a99-9e82-5c24-8f3c-8db058da3029" 17592186407359 "answer-baba48d0-d9fb-5842-84e6-6919f8e36cee" 17592186407360 "answer-cd6b9cf4-8a14-5d9c-8580-90b1f71a942c" 17592186407361 "answer-dbd0836e-e6f4-5b58-bfb5-c8dec7e9a94d" 17592186407362 "answer-f16a724b-c1f8-5ad0-8225-b9af9742e1cc" 17592186407363 "answer-f67abfd4-642f-5614-876f-390eb3d1595b" 17592186407364 "answer-fe963c24-be42-5cfe-a77e-8b918c0ffa49" 17592186407365 "answer-field-5c15890f-719b-5cd8-8053-341247002966" 17592186407366 "answer-field-6d1cab38-e87e-597f-87e0-47535946af67" 17592186407367 "question-82f2815d-a760-5a7e-b3a4-18ea182996e3" 17592186407368 "question-befb255b-f1bd-5c00-bc58-981c00e76ebb" 17592186407369} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
